        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=01.07">Chapter 01.07</a> Spokane Fair Elections Code</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.003">Section 01.07.003</a> Title;Purpose and Intent<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This chapter shall be titled and referred to as the Spokane Fair Elections Code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The purpose of this chapter is to institute regulations for the fair conduct of elections for citywide office and to ensure a high degree of transparency in the conduct of local elections. The City of Spokane is authorized to legislate in this area as a valid exercise of the City&rsquo;s police power, pursuant to Washington Constitution Art. XI, secs. 10 and 11 and RCW 35.22.020 and RCW&nbsp;35.22.195. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City intends, by enacting this chapter, to provide for transparency, fairness, accountability, and integrity in the conduct of elections for City office, to promote and increase political participation and the open discussion of issues, and to reduce the effect of financial contributions on the integrity of our elections and our government.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This chapter is intended to compliment and be consistent with chapter 42.17A RCW as enforced by the Washington State Public Disclosure Commission. In the event of a conflict between this chapter and chapter 42.17A RCW, state law controls.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The City of Spokane has a strong governmental interest in preventing corruption, and the appearance of corruption, in its political processes, such as the election of City officials.&nbsp; This chapter, by strengthening limits on political contributions, therefore serves the City&rsquo;s strong interests in preventing corruption and the appearance of corruption because it reduces the risk of <em>quid pro quo</em> arrangements and mitigates the appearance of corruption which is created by the real or potentially coercive influence of large financial contributions on the actions of candidates and elected officials.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It is the intent of the City Council to advocate for campaign finance reforms at the state and federal level. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.005">Section 01.07.005</a> Definitions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The definitions currently contained in RCW 42.17A.005 or as may be amended in the future are incorporated into Chapter 01.07 SMC by reference herein and are augmented by the following definitions:</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Agency&rdquo; means&nbsp;the City of Spokane internal auditor within the City&rsquo;s Department of Management and Budget or its delegate.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;City office&rdquo; means any elective office established by Section 5 of the Spokane City Charter, namely, Mayor, City Council member, and Municipal Court judge.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&ldquo;Collectively bargain&rdquo; means the performance of the mutual obligations of the public employer, including the City of Spokane or the Mayor, and the exclusive bargaining representative to meet at reasonable times, to confer and negotiate in good faith, and to execute a written agreement with respect to grievance procedures and collective negotiations on personnel matters, including wages, hours, and working conditions, which may be peculiar to an appropriate bargaining unit of the public employer, except that by such obligation neither party may be compelled to agree to a proposal or be required to make a concession unless otherwise allowed under Washington state law.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Contract&rdquo; has the same meaning as in SMC 07.06.040.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Contractor&rdquo; means&nbsp;<span style="background-color:white">any person or entity who has received the award of a contract under SMC 07.06.150 or SMC 07.06.160, submitted a bid or proposal in any form for the award of a contract under SMC 07.06.100, including any other person or entity who seeks the award of the contract and is contesting, appealing or protesting the award of the contract as proposed. The term includes sole proprietors, each general partner in a partnership, members of limited liability companies, and each corporate officer or shareholder holding a controlling interest in a corporation. The term shall also include any subcontractor authorized to provide all or a portion of goods, labor, or services in fulfillment of an award of a contract under SMC 07.06.150 or SMC 07.06.160. This definition does not include the employees of such a person or, if the person is a union, the members of that union.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Election for city office&rdquo; means any primary, general, or special election for city office as defined in this section.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">&ldquo;Entity&rdquo; means any business corporation, group, union, bargaining unit, agency, nonprofit corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company, and general cooperative association.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 12, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, October 26, 2022</p><p>ORD C36262 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.010">Section 01.07.010</a> Local Voters’ Pamphlet – Pro and Con Committee Statements<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Consistent with state law and the Spokane County auditor&rsquo;s administrative rules regarding participation in a local voters&rsquo; pamphlet as they currently exist or as may be amended, the Spokane City Council shall formally appoint by resolution a Pro Committee to prepare arguments advocating voters&rsquo; approval of a ballot measure and a Con Committee to prepare arguments advocating voters&rsquo; rejection of the measure. A Pro Committee established to prepare arguments advocating voters&rsquo; approval of a ballot measure submitted pursuant to an initiative or referendum shall include the sponsor or a representative of the sponsor of the initiative or referendum. A Con Committee established to prepare arguments advocating voters&rsquo; rejection of a ballot measure submitted pursuant to an initiative or referendum shall include a representative of any political committee opposing the measure that has filed a C-1 registration statement with the Washington Public Disclosure Commission.&nbsp; All committee members shall be registered voters in the city of Spokane.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Once established, the committees shall prepare arguments for and against local ballot measures to be included in the voters&rsquo; pamphlet consistent with state law and the Spokane County auditor&rsquo;s administrative rules.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="color:black"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If a local voters&rsquo; pamphlet is not published and distributed, the City shall participate with the Spokane County auditor&rsquo;s office in the posting of the election information on the County&rsquo;s website or on the City of Spokane&rsquo;s election resources page.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="margin-left: 0in; margin-right: 0in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif">&nbsp;<span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">For purposes of this section, the term &ldquo;measures&rdquo; includes all ballot measures placed on a local election ballot including measures submitted to the electorate pursuant to the City&rsquo;s initiative and referendum procedure.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.020">Section 01.07.020</a> Voter Registration & Election Resources<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Beginning with the first City of Spokane utility bill of the year in which a city general election is held, each utility bill shall include voter registration information and links to the Spokane County Elections Office and the Washington State Secretary of State websites.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City&rsquo;s website shall host a page devoted to election resources and clearly titled &ldquo;Voting and Elections&rdquo;. The site shall contain information and/or links to information including, but not limited to, voter registration, election dates, online voter pamphlets and guides, the Washington State Public Disclosure Commission, and ballot drop box locations. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City Clerk&rsquo;s Office shall be the city&rsquo;s election resources center and shall be the central location for any information related to city elections including, but not limited to, sample ballots, voter pamphlets and guides, and voter registration forms. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.030">Section 01.07.030</a> Mandatory Limitations on Campaign Contributions<br />
        <ol start="1" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A candidate for city office, and any political committee acting on behalf of such candidate, shall only accept or receive a campaign contribution during the election cycle in which the candidate will appear on the ballot.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Candidate filings with the Washington State Public Disclosure Commission shall constitute the evidence of contributions received during an election cycle for the purposes of enforcement of the penalty for violation.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 12, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, October 26, 2022</p><p>ORD C36262 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.040">Section 01.07.040</a> Prohibition on Campaign Contributions by Contractors<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No City of Spokane elected official or any candidate for city office, or any political committee acting on behalf of such elected official or candidate, shall knowingly solicit or accept any contribution directly or indirectly from any contractor who, in the two years prior to the election cycle has earned or received more than fifty thousand dollars ($50,000) under a contractual relationship with the City. No City of Spokane elected official, candidate for city office, or any political committee acting on behalf of an elected official or candidate for such office, shall knowingly solicit a contribution for himself or herself or for any political party, political committee, incidental committee, or campaign committee, directly or indirectly from any contractor who in the prior two years has earned or received more than fifty thousand dollars ($50,000) under a contractual relationship with the City. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No City of Spokane elected official, candidate for city office, or any political committee acting on behalf of an elected official or candidate of such office, shall knowingly solicit or accept any contribution from a contractor during a contract award period. If a City of Spokane elected official or candidate for city office or a political committee acting on their behalf unknowingly accepts a contribution from a contractor during a contract award period, it shall be the duty of the elected official or candidate for such position or political committee acting on their behalf to return the contribution within ten (10) days after he or she becomes aware of the violation. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It is a violation of this chapter for a contractor or its subsidiary(ies), parent company or affiliate(s), to reimburse an employee, officer, director, or partner of such contractor for political contributions in support of a candidate for city office.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Contributions made or solicited prior to the effective date of this ordinance is not a violation of this ordinance. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The receipt of legal campaign contributions by the Mayor, member of the Spokane City Council, a Municipal Court Judge, or a candidate for city office shall not be considered a conflict of interest as defined by Spokane Municipal Code 01.4A.030 when approving and executing contracts on behalf of the City of Spokane. </span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.050">Section 01.07.050</a> Disclosure of Campaign Contributions by City Bargaining Units<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All entities who collectively bargain with the City of Spokane on behalf of its membership shall submit information on all bargaining unit contracts prior to signatures and approval by the City Council listing the dollar value of campaign contributions donated to any current City of Spokane elected official, the dollar value of campaign contributions donated to a political committee acting on behalf of a current elected official or has donated to any current City of Spokane elected official or has made independent expenditures in support or against any current City of Spokane elected official, or the dollar amount of the campaign contributions given to an incidental committee that has given campaign contributions to any current City of Spokane elected official or has made independent expenditures in support or opposition to any current City of Spokane elected official.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The receipt of legal campaign contributions by the Mayor, a member of the Spokane City Council, or a Municipal Court Judge shall not be considered a conflict of interest as defined by SMC 01.4A.030 when approving and executing bargaining agreement contracts on behalf of the City of Spokane. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.060">Section 01.07.060</a> Identification of Contributors Required<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any entity that makes campaign contributions to a candidate for city office, independent expenditures for or against a candidate for city office, or for or against a City ballot measure shall have an active registration with the Washington Secretary of State or equivalent state agency of the donors&rsquo; headquarters or primary location. </span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.070">Section 01.07.070</a> Disclosure by Political Committees<br />
        <ol start="1" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li>In addition to the requirements of RCW 42.17A.320, a political committee making independent expenditures in support or opposition to a candidate for city office or in support or against a City of Spokane initiative or referendum shall identify the three persons or entities making the largest contributions in excess of five hundred dollars ($500) during the twelve-month period preceding the date on which the advertisement is initially to be published or otherwise presented to the public.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li>For any political committee or incidental committee that qualifies as one of the top three contributors identified under (a) of this section, the top three contributors to that political committee or incidental committee during the same period shall be identified, and so on, until the individuals or entities other than political committees or incidental committees that have contributed the most to all political committees or incidental committees involved with the advertisement have been identified.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 12, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, October 26, 2022</p><p>ORD C36262 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.080">Section 01.07.080</a> REPEALED (Contributions by Incidental Committees)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 12, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, October 26, 2022</p><p>ORD C36262 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.090">Section 01.07.090</a> Contributions by Foreign-Owned Corporations<br />
        <p><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All entities making contributions to City of Spokane elected officials or any candidate for city office, or any political committee acting on behalf of such elected official or candidate shall provide certification to the receipt of the donation at the time of the donation that the entity is not a foreign-owned entity as defined by SMC 01.07.005(S).</span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.100">Section 01.07.100</a> REPEALED (Complaints and Investigations – Curing of Violations; Process)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 12, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, October 26, 2022</p><p>ORD C36262 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.110">Section 01.07.110</a> Enforcement<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Unless otherwise specified herein, violation of the requirements of this chapter is a civil infraction.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each day in which a person remains in violation of SMC 01.07.030, 01.070.040, 01.07.060, 01.07.080, or 01.07.090 constitutes a separate civil infraction.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each communication made in violation of SMC 01.07.070 constitutes a separate civil infraction. For purposes of this section, &ldquo;communication&rdquo; means the sending of a single piece of direct mail or the actual airing of a single radio, television, or digital video advertisement.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If the Agency determines, pursuant to, that a violation of this chapter has occurred or is occurring, the Agency shall refer the matter to the City Attorney&rsquo;s or City Prosecutor&rsquo;s office for the filing of a civil infraction(s) pursuant to chapter 01.05, SMC. In any action brought to enforce this chapter, the court may order the return of any contributions received in violation of this chapter, and the city may recover all costs of investigation, in addition to any other remedies allowed by law.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">When referring an enforcement action to the City Attorneys&rsquo; office or City Prosecutor&rsquo;s office, the Agency shall also notify the person subject to the Notice of Violation that they are ineligible to receive contributions until such person comes into compliance with this chapter or until the matter is determined by the Municipal Court, whichever occurs first.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 24, 2025</p><p>ORD C36702 Section 11</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.120">Section 01.07.120</a> Limitations Period<br />
        <p><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A person filing a complaint under </span></span> <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=01.07.100" target="_blank">SMC 01.07.100</a> <span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">may do so only until May 31 of the year following the election cycle to which the complaint pertains. It is an affirmative defense to any enforcement action taken under this chapter that the complaint was filed beyond the limitation period stated in this section. By way of illustration only, a complaint alleging a violation of this chapter which occurred in 2019 must, in order to be timely, be filed on or before May 31, 2020.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.130">Section 01.07.130</a> Publicity<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Agency shall, in conjunction with the City Clerk&rsquo;s office, publish on the City&rsquo;s website in a location in common with all other election resources:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each NOV issued by the Agency, including the date of issuance, identity of both the complaining person and the person alleged to have violated this chapter, and the final disposition of the NOV;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Notices of ineligibility for contributions required under <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=01.07.110">SMC 01.07.110(D)</a>, including the beginning and end dates of the ineligibility; and</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The additional disclosures permitted under <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=01.07.100">SMC 01.07.100(C)</a> to cure a violation of this chapter.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.140">Section 01.07.140</a> Severability<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">If a court of law determines that any provision of this chapter is void or of no legal effect, the offending provision(s) shall be deemed struck from this chapter and the remainder of the chapter shall continue unaffected.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.07.150">Section 01.07.150</a> Annual Reporting<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Beginning in 2019 and on an annual basis thereafter, the Agency shall make a report to the City Council and shall cause a copy of that report to be posted on the City&rsquo;s election resources web page, concerning the number and type of complaints made, investigations undertaken, and actions taken to enforce the provisions of this chapter. </span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 8, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 7, 2018</p><p>ORD C35571 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=01.08">Chapter 01.08</a> REPEALED (Acquisition and Use of Surveillance Equipment)</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.010">Section 01.08.010</a> REPEALED (Definitions)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.020">Section 01.08.020</a> REPEALED (City Council Approval for City Department Acquisition and Operations of Surveillance Equipment)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.030">Section 01.08.030</a> REPEALED (Data Management Protocols for Surveillance Equipment)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.040">Section 01.08.040</a> REPEALED (Acquisition and Use of Surveillance Equipment Related to Law Enforcement Investigations)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.050">Section 01.08.050</a> REPEALED (Prior Use of Surveillance Equipment)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=01.08.060">Section 01.08.060</a> REPEALED (Application to City Contractors and Agents)<br />
        <p>
        	Repealed by ORD C35485 Section 1<o:p></o:p></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 1</p></form>
        </div>
